# Agenda de aulas

Alunos marcam aulas e o professor confirma.

Stack: React Native (Expo).

## Run it locally

### Prerequisites

- Node.js
- Git
- Expo Go on your phone

### Step by step

1. Clone the repository and enter the folder:
   ```bash
   git clone https://github.com/you/agenda-de-aulas.git
   cd agenda-de-aulas
   ```
2. Install the dependencies:
   ```bash
   npm install
   ```
3. Copy the variables and fill in the values:
   ```bash
   cp .env.example .env
   ```
4. Run the app and scan the QR code with Expo Go:
   ```bash
   npx expo start
   ```

### Environment variables

| Variable | What it is for | Where to get it |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL` | API address. Ships inside the app: anyone can read it. | Example: `https://api.exemplo.com` |
| `EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` | Supabase project address, if it is the chosen back end. | Example: `https://xxxx.supabase.co` |
| `EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` | Supabase public key; can ship in the app because access is controlled by database rules. | Example: `(chave pública do painel)` |

No secret value is kept in the repository: fill in secrets only in your .env.

## Folder structure

| Folder | What it holds |
| --- | --- |
| `src/app/` | Screens; each file becomes a route (Expo Router). |
| `src/components/` | Reusable interface pieces. |
| `src/lib/` | API and local storage access. |
| `assets/` | Icon, splash screen and images. |
| `app.json` | App name, icon and permissions. |

